				1
			],
			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "a15387c29c3ea0495a9b3f060d0da6ad13632eb2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T01:46:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				221,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add ExposeWorkbenchAccessor transform plugin\n\nAdd a new ESBuild transform plugin that patches VS Code's web.main.js\nand web.factory.js to expose the workbench's IInstantiationService and\nIWorkbench facade on globalThis. This enables Sky-side bridge code to\nresolve internal services (IStatusbarService, ISCMService, ICommandService,\netc.) via __CEL_INSTANTIATION_SERVICE__.invokeFunction() without\nre-implementing a parallel UI surface.\n\nThe transform makes two narrow additive patches:\n1. web.main.js - after workbench.startup(), stash the live\n   IInstantiationService on globalThis.__CEL_INSTANTIATION_SERVICE__\n2. web.factory.js - after workbenchPromise.complete(), expose the IWorkbench\n   facade on globalThis.__CEL_WORKBENCH__ and dispatch cel:workbench-ready\n\nBoth injections are idempotent (short-circuit on existing marker) so\nre-running the transform on an already-patched tree is a no-op.",
			"SHA": "358449c0d10f262c5b4869d7088c5a0ccf2a9f23"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T00:08:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠃⠀⠀⠀",
				218,
				55
			],
			"Message": "build(Output): Remove Configuration source directory\n\nDelete the entire Configuration/Source directory from the Output element. This includes ESBuild configs, TypeScript configs, build plugins, polyfills, and service modules.\n\nThe Output element should contain only the final bundled JS artifacts consumed by Cocoon at runtime, not source build configuration files. These configuration files should be regenerated from their source definitions during the build process.",
			"SHA": "51de686e76fe8bbdaf8c8bca938d3d79fc793522"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T00:08:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				290,
				55
			],
			"Message": "revert(Output): Restore Configuration build directory\n\nThe previous commit removed the Configuration directory as \"intermediate artifacts\", but these are actually source configuration files (ESBuild configs, TypeScript configs, build plugins, polyfills, and service modules) that define how the VS Code source is transformed for Land.\n\nThese files were incorrectly classified as intermediate build artifacts. They are essential source configurations that:\n- Define ESBuild bundling rules for CodeEditorLand/Editor and Microsoft/VSCode targets\n- Provide TypeScript compilation configs with proper path mappings\n- Implement build plugins for code transformation (IPC shims, CSS handling, electron replacements)\n- Supply browser polyfills (fs, child_process, ipcRenderer, etc.)\n- Define Tauri main process service stubs\n\nThe Output element requires these configuration files to produce the bundled JS artifacts consumed by Cocoon at runtime.",
			"SHA": "9ea46755c9ab13a25e53afb3b1929eaf801db7ff"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1781048774234
}